 "method": "Every work read as a monophonic line per part. Intervals are signed semitone steps between consecutive notes in one voice; shares are of all melodic moves pooled across the corpus. Devices and unexplained dissonances come from tools/counterpoint/rules.py profile free, so these targets and the cue gate are the same measurement. Cadences are chord-pair readings: dominant to tonic, subdominant to tonic, dominant to submediant, and phrases that stop on the dominant at a rest. Sequences are 4-interval cells that recur at a new pitch inside a voice. Imitation is the same cell in another voice starting later and within four bars. Nothing melodic is stored here; every field is a count or a share.",
